; The [(load "FILE")] search order (design D3), shared by the two executables
; that resolve loads — the `pol` command line and the LSP process.
;
; It has its own library precisely because it was duplicated once and drifted:
; the editor searched the document's directory then [lib/], while the command
; line searched design D3's four places. [core/stdlib] was in one list and not
; the other, so `pol check` passed on a model whose buffer showed a red error.
; One copy, linked by both, is what makes that class of divergence impossible.
;
; Computing the candidate paths is ALL this library does — reading them is I/O
; and stays in the two executables, so the rule that they are the only modules
; touching a file descriptor is untouched.

(library
 (name pol_loadpath)
 (libraries pol_data))
